igin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $100$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =100 \\\\ \\frac{25{y}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{100} & =\\frac{100}{100} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10438/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7c76e6-204b-5b30-8e62-c53027b63448"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975/selection/d08454869fa7921cf250e16ac34885e4d364aa34a8406650c81c81d7dba982bc" :answer/id #uuid "a6ef0a70-c2dc-598d-90e2-476419bc2fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{8}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975/selection/241d7f4e546f231146c45879647fbc0d9ba1003e4f509d0800db9e8a54ece31e" :answer/id #uuid "51e077dd-de0c-5b47-87d2-109fe8974023" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975/selection/2fec67784a2f686bc9fece296edf9221da324dc0e34cbf29534c18c8d58f2ba4" :answer/id #uuid "7eb55387-fd0b-5750-ae9e-5e83e8811bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975/selection/bbe5e63917119ee7237fdd695e959c25e33b08f6f04aa7a4e3856421aa97d053" :answer/id #uuid "28ea1c25-d9d6-50cf-b252-2efb120d000d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975/selection/b8b02456486afaaf9fa5a88ff252016c8e4510cef18af6e19199674056f6ddbc" :answer/id #uuid "8fa4402e-7edb-50be-a242-304c11e8456d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc80fba-216c-5094-9c66-4f0f64d3d0fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7975/selection/241d7f4e546f231146c45879647fbc0d9ba1003e4f509d0800db9e8a54ece31e" :answer-field/choices ["q-7975/selection/d08454869fa7921cf250e16ac34885e4d364aa34a8406650c81c81d7dba982bc" "q-7975/selection/241d7f4e546f231146c45879647fbc0d9ba1003e4f509d0800db9e8a54ece31e" "q-7975/selection/2fec67784a2f686bc9fece296edf9221da324dc0e34cbf29534c18c8d58f2ba4" "q-7975/selection/bbe5e63917119ee7237fdd695e959c25e33b08f6f04aa7a4e3856421aa97d053" "q-7975/selection/b8b02456486afaaf9fa5a88ff252016c8e4510cef18af6e19199674056f6ddbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7975" :question/id #uuid "2f6002f1-8240-53b8-b0d9-a0d60eeea0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-7975" :question/problem "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}=400.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $400$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{400}-\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{400} & =\\frac{400}{400} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{16}=4,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7975/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7c76e6-204b-5b30-8e62-c53027b63448"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7975"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316934/field-1/7b884fe358afd17ba06829f205b975d5f748211a8cda12818b551788bb36e483" :answer/id #uuid "b79ec82a-19e5-5c35-9748-8b3e3d2fdce9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316934/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c023e27d-0697-5e56-9631-a075d0105484" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316934/field-1/7b884fe358afd17ba06829f205b975d5f748211a8cda12818b551788bb36e483" :answer-field/choices ["q-316934/field-1/7b884fe358afd17ba06829f205b975d5f748211a8cda12818b551788bb36e483"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316934" :question/id #uuid "a9dee5e2-9b78-5b62-a5a4-664e0882321f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316934" :question/problem "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $8{x}^{2}-50{y}^{2}=400$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $400$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}-50{y}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{8{x}^{2}}{400}-\\frac{50{y}^{2}}{400} & =\\frac{400}{400} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{50}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{50}$ and $b=\\sqrt{8}.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{50}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{5\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316934/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7c76e6-204b-5b30-8e62-c53027b63448"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316934"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7426"] :question/problem "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{36} = 6, \\qquad b=\\sqrt9 =3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{6}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5356"] :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b} x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y = \\pm \\dfrac{3}{4}x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5357"] :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $225$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{225}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{225} & =\\frac{225}{225} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt 9 = 3,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{5}{3}x.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
